The Service Provider shall:

- Provide Services in accordance with the terms and conditions of this Agreement;
- Use reasonable skill, care, and diligence in the performance of the Services;
- Keep confidential all information obtained in the course of providing the Services;
- Comply with all applicable laws and regulations;
- Not assign, sub-contract, or delegate the provision of the Services without prior written consent of the Client;
- Indemnify and hold harmless the Client against all claims, damages, and expenses arising from the provision of the Services; and
- Remediate any defects or issues in the Services within a reasonable timeframe.

The Client shall:

- Provide timely and accurate information to the Service Provider as necessary for the provision of the Services;
- Pay all fees and charges for the Services in accordance with the payment terms of this Agreement;
- Use the Services only for lawful purposes;
- Comply with all applicable laws and regulations;
- Not assign, sub-contract, or delegate the use of the Services without prior written consent of the Service Provider; and
- Not interfere with the Service Provider's performance of the Services.

Dispute resolution will be governed by the laws of the jurisdiction where the Service Provider is incorporated. Any disputes or claims arising from this Agreement will be resolved through binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the relevant arbitration association.

The Client agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the Service Provider, its officers, directors, employees, contractors, and agents, from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees and costs) arising out of, resulting from, or in any way connected with:

- The Client's use of the Services;
- The Client's breach of this Agreement;
- The Client's violation of any applicable law or regulation;
- Any third-party claim or dispute arising from the Client's use of the Services or the Client's breach of this Agreement.

The Client shall promptly notify the Service Provider in writing of any claim or action made against the Client that may give rise to a demand or claim against the Service Provider, and shall cooperate with the Service Provider in the defense of any such claim or action.

ARTICLE 10: INDEMNIFICATION AND HOLD HARMLESS

10.1 Each party (the "Indemnifying Party") shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other party (the "Indemnitee"), its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates (collectively, the "Indemnitee's Related Parties") from and against any and all third-party claims, demands, actions, causes of action, suits, liabilities, damages, losses, costs, and expenses (including, without limitation, reasonable attorneys' fees and expenses) (collectively, the "Losses") arising out of or related to:

10.1.1 any breach by the Indemnifying Party of any of its obligations under this Agreement;

10.1.2 any negligence or willful misconduct by the Indemnifying Party;

10.1.3 the provision of the services by the Indemnifying Party;

10.1.4 the use of the services by the Indemnitee;

10.1.5 any claim of infringement of any intellectual property rights of any third party;

10.1.6 any claim of defamation or libel;

10.1.7 any claim arising out of or related to the Indemnitee's use of the services, including, without limitation, any claims arising out of or related to viruses, Trojan horses, or other malicious software.

10.2 The Indemnifying Party shall not be required to indemnify the Indemnitee for any Losses arising out of or related to:

10.2.1 any claim that is based on the Indemnitee's gross negligence or willful misconduct;

10.2.2 any claim that is based on the Indemnitee's non-compliance with applicable laws and regulations;

10.2.3 any claim that is based on the Indemnitee's failure to provide accurate or complete information;

10.2.4 any claim that is based on the Indemnitee's failure to maintain the security and integrity of the services.

10.3 The Indemnitee shall promptly notify the Indemnifying Party of any claim that may give rise to Losses. The Indemnifying Party shall have the right to control the defense of any claim, and the Indemnitee shall cooperate with the Indemnifying Party in the defense of any claim.

10.4 The indemnification obligations set forth in this Article 10 shall be in addition to and supersede any other indemnification obligations set forth in this Agreement.

10.5 The provisions of this Article 10 shall survive the expiration or termination of this Agreement and shall continue in full force and effect.
